"A sea cave opens in Gullrock Head's seaward foot, dry to walk into only at low tide."
"Low tide falls around dawn and again around dusk; at high tide the cave mouth is under the surf."
"At the back of the sea cave a stone arch carved with worn sea shapes leads down stairs into the dark."
"The arch is the way into the Salt Halls; the System names it when she first nears it."
"The broken hull of a small ship of no Earth make lies wedged in the rocks on Gullrock Head's north side."
"The wreck is old; its crew is long gone, and the sea has taken most of its cargo."
"In the wreck's hold a swollen sea trunk holds sailcloth, a coil of tarred rope and a hand axe."
"Under the trunk's cloth is a pair of soft leather sea boots, far too big for Nala."
"A clay jar in the wreck's galley still holds a pint of stale fresh water under its wax seal."
